/E (secure financial transactions, control the creation of new units, and verify the transfer of assets. Unlike traditional currencies issued by central banks, cryptocurrencies are decentralized. They operate on blockchain technology, a distributed ledger enforced by a network of computers called nodes. The first cryptocurrency, Bitcoin, was introduced in 2009 by an anonymous entity known as Satoshi Nakamoto. It opened a new avenue for peer-to-peer electronic cash transactions, freeing them from the control of any government or institution. Today, thousands of cryptocurrencies exist, each with unique attributes and uses.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [13]
>>
